    "node_id": "I_kwDORdC75M8AAAABMGJiGQ",
    "title": "[bug] --kind silently selects among duplicate same-kind symbols",
    "body": "## Description\n\nPassing `--kind` can silently select the first result when multiple exact-name candidates have the same requested kind. Because resolution completes before ambiguity handling, an accompanying `--pick` is ignored as well.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n1. Create two TypeScript files that each export a class named `DuplicateService`.\n2. Give the first class one member and the second class two members so the selected target is observable.\n3. Run `ix map . --silent`.\n4. Run `ix impact DuplicateService --kind class --format json`.\n5. Run `ix impact DuplicateService --kind class --pick 2 --format json`.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n`--kind class` should filter out other kinds but remain ambiguous when multiple classes still match. Adding `--pick 2` should select the second class.\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nBoth commands silently select the first class and report one member. The second command ignores `--pick 2`.\n\nWithout `--kind`, the same fixture correctly reports both candidates:\n\n```text\nAmbiguous symbol \"DuplicateService\":\n  1. class ... DuplicateService in src/alpha/DuplicateService.ts\n  2. class ... DuplicateService in src/beta/DuplicateService.ts\n```\n\n## CLI output\n\n```json\n{\n  \"resolvedTarget\": {\n    \"kind\": \"class\",\n    \"name\": \"DuplicateService\"\n  },\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"members\": 1\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe output remains the same with `--kind class --pick 2`, although the second class has two members.\n\n## Environment\n- OS: macOS 26.6.1\n- Node: 26.7.0\n- Ix version: 0.9.1 and current `main`\n",
    "state": "closed",
    "state_reason": "completed",
